@startuml
title Durable run lifecycle on the public ledger
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "running" as running #E9F5EA
state "suspended" as suspended #FFF0D9
state "resuming" as resuming #FFE0C8
state "completed" as completed #D9EFDF
state "failed" as failed #F8DADA
state "cancelled" as cancelled #E7DCF5
state "returned" as returned #F2F2F2 ##[dashed]888888

[*] --> running : registerRun + beginDurableRun\n(runStarted)
running --> suspended : advanceRun\n(runSuspended / durableYield / retryScheduled)
suspended --> resuming : claimCommand\n(commandClaimed, revision CAS)
resuming --> running : advanceRun\n(runResumed)
resuming --> suspended : clearCommand\n(commandRejected)
running --> completed : advanceRun\n(runCompleted)
running --> failed : advanceRun\n(runFailed)
running --> cancelled : advanceRun\n(runCancelled)
suspended --> cancelled : cancel command\n(cancellationRequested ... runCancelled)
running --> running : migrate command\n(runMigrated: rebind definition hash)
suspended --> suspended : migrate command\n(runMigrated)
completed --> [*]
failed --> [*]
cancelled --> [*]
completed -[#888888,dashed]-> returned : finishRun (legacy run.rho only)\n(runReturned)
returned -[#888888,dashed]-> [*]

note right of resuming #FFF3C9
Every advancement is a compare-and-set on the
run revision: <latex>\nu' = \nu + 1</latex> with the claimed
command cleared. A replayed advancement is
acknowledged idempotently by exact readback.
end note
note bottom of returned #F2F2F2
Legacy status: only the non-durable run.rho
template calls finishRun. Durable runs end at
completed, failed, or cancelled.
end note
note left of suspended #EAF7EE
The ledger publishes sorted wait ids, the minimum
due_at, and approval authority grants for every
suspension; payloads stay encrypted in F1r3drive.
end note
@enduml
